1. Attribution

Any public or private distribution of the Work, or of a derivative work based
on the Work, must include clear and reasonably visible attribution to the
original Speechless project and its original author.

At a minimum, such attribution must include:

- the project name: "Speechless"
- a statement that the work is based on or derived from Speechless
- a link to the original repository when technically and commercially
  reasonable to provide

2. Shareback

If you distribute, deploy, commercialize, sublicense, offer as a hosted
service, or otherwise make available a modified or derivative version of the
Work, you must make the source code of your modifications available to the
original project maintainers, and you are expected to contribute those
modifications back to the upstream Speechless project in a reasonable form,
such as a pull request, patch set, or source archive.

3. No removal of notices

You may not remove, obscure, or falsify copyright, attribution, or license
notices contained in the Work.

4. No trademark grant

This license does not grant any right to use the names, branding, logos, or
trademarks of the original project except as required for truthful attribution.

5. Ideas and concepts

To the extent allowed by law, users of this Work are asked to preserve
attribution not only to the code itself but also to the underlying product
